{"book":"II Kings","chapter":7,"entries":[{"id":9708,"title":"II Kings 7:1","segments":["¶Then Elisha said, Hear ye the word of the LORD; Thus saith the LORD, To morrow about this time [shall] a measure of fine flour [be sold] for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria."],"ref":"II Kings 7:1","verse":1,"words":[{"text":"¶Then Elisha","strong":"H477"},{"text":" said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Hear","strong":"H8085"},{"text":" ye the word","strong":"H1697"},{"text":" of the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":"; Thus saith","strong":"H559"},{"text":" the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":", To morrow","strong":"H4279"},{"text":" about this time","strong":"H6256"},{"text":" [shall] a measure","strong":"H5429"},{"text":" of fine flour","strong":"H5560"},{"text":" [be sold] for a shekel","strong":"H8255"},{"text":", and two measures","strong":"H5429"},{"text":" of barley","strong":"H8184"},{"text":" for a shekel","strong":"H8255"},{"text":", in the gate","strong":"H8179"},{"text":" of Samaria","strong":"H8111"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9709,"title":"II Kings 7:2","segments":["Then a lord on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, Behold, [if] the LORD would make windows in heaven, might this thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see [it] with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof. {a lord...: Heb. a lord which belonged to the king leaning upon his hand}"],"ref":"II Kings 7:2","verse":2,"words":[{"text":"Then a lord","strong":"H7991"},{"text":" on whose hand","strong":"H3027"},{"text":" the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" leaned","strong":"H8172"},{"text":" answered","strong":"H6030"},{"text":" the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":", and said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Behold, [if] the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" would make","strong":"H6213"},{"text":" windows","strong":"H699"},{"text":" in heaven","strong":"H8064"},{"text":", might this thing","strong":"H1697"},{"text":" be? And he said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Behold, thou shalt see","strong":"H7200"},{"text":" [it] with thine eyes","strong":"H5869"},{"text":", but shalt not eat","strong":"H398"},{"text":" thereof. {a lord...: Heb. a lord which belonged to the king leaning upon his hand}"}]},{"id":9710,"title":"II Kings 7:3","segments":["¶And there were four leprous men at the entering in of the gate: and they said one to another, Why sit we here until we die?"],"ref":"II Kings 7:3","verse":3,"words":[{"text":"¶And there were four","strong":"H702"},{"text":" leprous","strong":"H6879"},{"text":" men","strong":"H582"},{"text":" at the entering in","strong":"H6607"},{"text":" of the gate","strong":"H8179"},{"text":": and they said","strong":"H559"},{"text":" one","strong":"H376"},{"text":" to another","strong":"H7453"},{"text":", Why sit","strong":"H3427"},{"text":" we here until we die","strong":"H4191"},{"text":"?"}]},{"id":9711,"title":"II Kings 7:4","segments":["If we say, We will enter into the city, then the famine [is] in the city, and we shall die there: and if we sit still here, we die also. Now therefore come, and let us fall unto the host of the Syrians: if they save us alive, we shall live; and if they kill us, we shall but die."],"ref":"II Kings 7:4","verse":4,"words":[{"text":"If we say","strong":"H559"},{"text":", We will enter","strong":"H935"},{"text":" into the city","strong":"H5892"},{"text":", then the famine","strong":"H7458"},{"text":" [is] in the city","strong":"H5892"},{"text":", and we shall die","strong":"H4191"},{"text":" there: and if we sit still","strong":"H3427"},{"text":" here, we die","strong":"H4191"},{"text":" also. Now therefore come","strong":"H3212"},{"text":", and let us fall","strong":"H5307"},{"text":" unto the host","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":": if they save us alive","strong":"H2421"},{"text":", we shall live","strong":"H2421"},{"text":"; and if they kill","strong":"H4191"},{"text":" us, we shall but die","strong":"H4191"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9712,"title":"II Kings 7:5","segments":["And they rose up in the twilight, to go unto the camp of the Syrians: and when they were come to the uttermost part of the camp of Syria, behold, [there was] no man there."],"ref":"II Kings 7:5","verse":5,"words":[{"text":"And they rose up","strong":"H6965"},{"text":" in the twilight","strong":"H5399"},{"text":", to go","strong":"H935"},{"text":" unto the camp","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":": and when they were come","strong":"H935"},{"text":" to the uttermost part","strong":"H7097"},{"text":" of the camp","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of Syria","strong":"H758"},{"text":", behold, [there was] no man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" there."}]},{"id":9713,"title":"II Kings 7:6","segments":["For the Lord had made the host of the Syrians to hear a noise of chariots, and a noise of horses, [even] the noise of a great host: and they said one to another, Lo, the king of Israel hath hired against us the kings of the Hittites, and the kings of the Egyptians, to come upon us."],"ref":"II Kings 7:6","verse":6,"words":[{"text":"For the Lord","strong":"H136"},{"text":" had made the host","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":" to hear","strong":"H8085"},{"text":" a noise","strong":"H6963"},{"text":" of chariots","strong":"H7393"},{"text":", and a noise","strong":"H6963"},{"text":" of horses","strong":"H5483"},{"text":", [even] the noise","strong":"H6963"},{"text":" of a great","strong":"H1419"},{"text":" host","strong":"H2428"},{"text":": and they said","strong":"H559"},{"text":" one","strong":"H376"},{"text":" to another","strong":"H251"},{"text":", Lo, the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" of Israel","strong":"H3478"},{"text":" hath hired","strong":"H7936"},{"text":" against us the kings","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" of the Hittites","strong":"H2850"},{"text":", and the kings","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" of the Egyptians","strong":"H4714"},{"text":", to come","strong":"H935"},{"text":" upon us."}]},{"id":9714,"title":"II Kings 7:7","segments":["Wherefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, and their horses, and their asses, even the camp as it [was], and fled for their life."],"ref":"II Kings 7:7","verse":7,"words":[{"text":"Wherefore they arose","strong":"H6965"},{"text":" and fled","strong":"H5127"},{"text":" in the twilight","strong":"H5399"},{"text":", and left","strong":"H5800"},{"text":" their tents","strong":"H168"},{"text":", and their horses","strong":"H5483"},{"text":", and their asses","strong":"H2543"},{"text":", even the camp","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" as it [was], and fled","strong":"H5127"},{"text":" for their life","strong":"H5315"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9715,"title":"II Kings 7:8","segments":["And when these lepers came to the uttermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and did eat and drink, and carried thence silver, and gold, and raiment, and went and hid [it]; and came again, and entered into another tent, and carried thence [also], and went and hid [it]."],"ref":"II Kings 7:8","verse":8,"words":[{"text":"And when these lepers","strong":"H6879"},{"text":" came","strong":"H935"},{"text":" to the uttermost part","strong":"H7097"},{"text":" of the camp","strong":"H4264"},{"text":", they went","strong":"H935"},{"text":" into one","strong":"H259"},{"text":" tent","strong":"H168"},{"text":", and did eat","strong":"H398"},{"text":" and drink","strong":"H8354"},{"text":", and carried","strong":"H5375"},{"text":" thence silver","strong":"H3701"},{"text":", and gold","strong":"H2091"},{"text":", and raiment","strong":"H899"},{"text":", and went","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" and hid","strong":"H2934"},{"text":" [it]; and came again","strong":"H7725"},{"text":", and entered","strong":"H935"},{"text":" into another","strong":"H312"},{"text":" tent","strong":"H168"},{"text":", and carried","strong":"H5375"},{"text":" thence [also], and went","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" and hid","strong":"H2934"},{"text":" [it]."}]},{"id":9716,"title":"II Kings 7:9","segments":["Then they said one to another, We do not well: this day [is] a day of good tidings, and we hold our peace: if we tarry till the morning light, some mischief will come upon us: now therefore come, that we may go and tell the king's household. {some...: Heb. we shall find punishment}"],"ref":"II Kings 7:9","verse":9,"words":[{"text":"Then they said","strong":"H559"},{"text":" one","strong":"H376"},{"text":" to another","strong":"H7453"},{"text":", We do","strong":"H6213"},{"text":" not well: this day","strong":"H3117"},{"text":" [is] a day","strong":"H3117"},{"text":" of good tidings","strong":"H1309"},{"text":", and we hold our peace","strong":"H2814"},{"text":": if we tarry","strong":"H2442"},{"text":" till the morning","strong":"H1242"},{"text":" light","strong":"H216"},{"text":", some mischief","strong":"H5771"},{"text":" will come","strong":"H4672"},{"text":" upon us: now therefore come","strong":"H3212"},{"text":", that we may go","strong":"H935"},{"text":" and tell","strong":"H5046"},{"text":" the king's","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" household","strong":"H1004"},{"text":". {some...: Heb. we shall find punishment}"}]},{"id":9717,"title":"II Kings 7:10","segments":["So they came and called unto the porter of the city: and they told them, saying, We came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, [there was] no man there, neither voice of man, but horses tied, and asses tied, and the tents as they [were]."],"ref":"II Kings 7:10","verse":10,"words":[{"text":"So they came","strong":"H935"},{"text":" and called","strong":"H7121"},{"text":" unto the porter","strong":"H7778"},{"text":" of the city","strong":"H5892"},{"text":": and they told","strong":"H5046"},{"text":" them, saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", We came","strong":"H935"},{"text":" to the camp","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":", and, behold, [there was] no man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" there, neither voice","strong":"H6963"},{"text":" of man","strong":"H120"},{"text":", but horses","strong":"H5483"},{"text":" tied","strong":"H631"},{"text":", and asses","strong":"H2543"},{"text":" tied","strong":"H631"},{"text":", and the tents","strong":"H168"},{"text":" as they [were]."}]},{"id":9718,"title":"II Kings 7:11","segments":["And he called the porters; and they told [it] to the king's house within."],"ref":"II Kings 7:11","verse":11,"words":[{"text":"And he called","strong":"H7121"},{"text":" the porters","strong":"H7778"},{"text":"; and they told","strong":"H5046"},{"text":" [it] to the king's","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" house","strong":"H1004"},{"text":" within","strong":"H6441"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9719,"title":"II Kings 7:12","segments":["¶And the king arose in the night, and said unto his servants, I will now shew you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we [be] hungry; therefore are they gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, When they come out of the city, we shall catch them alive, and get into the city."],"ref":"II Kings 7:12","verse":12,"words":[{"text":"¶And the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" arose","strong":"H6965"},{"text":" in the night","strong":"H3915"},{"text":", and said","strong":"H559"},{"text":" unto his servants","strong":"H5650"},{"text":", I will now shew","strong":"H5046"},{"text":" you what the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":" have done","strong":"H6213"},{"text":" to us. They know","strong":"H3045"},{"text":" that we [be] hungry","strong":"H7457"},{"text":"; therefore are they gone out","strong":"H3318"},{"text":" of the camp","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" to hide","strong":"H2247"},{"text":" themselves in the field","strong":"H7704"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", When they come out","strong":"H3318"},{"text":" of the city","strong":"H5892"},{"text":", we shall catch","strong":"H8610"},{"text":" them alive","strong":"H2416"},{"text":", and get","strong":"H935"},{"text":" into the city","strong":"H5892"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9720,"title":"II Kings 7:13","segments":["And one of his servants answered and said, Let [some] take, I pray thee, five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city, (behold, they [are] as all the multitude of Israel that are left in it: behold, [I say], they [are] even as all the multitude of the Israelites that are consumed:) and let us send and see. {in the city: Heb. in it}"],"ref":"II Kings 7:13","verse":13,"words":[{"text":"And one","strong":"H259"},{"text":" of his servants","strong":"H5650"},{"text":" answered","strong":"H6030"},{"text":" and said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Let [some] take","strong":"H3947"},{"text":", I pray thee, five","strong":"H2568"},{"text":" of the horses","strong":"H5483"},{"text":" that remain","strong":"H7604"},{"text":", which are left","strong":"H7604"},{"text":" in the city, (behold, they [are] as all the multitude","strong":"H1995"},{"text":" of Israel","strong":"H3478"},{"text":" that are left","strong":"H7604"},{"text":" in it: behold, [I say], they [are] even as all the multitude","strong":"H1995"},{"text":" of the Israelites","strong":"H3478"},{"text":" that are consumed","strong":"H8552"},{"text":":) and let us send","strong":"H7971"},{"text":" and see","strong":"H7200"},{"text":". {in the city: Heb. in it}"}]},{"id":9721,"title":"II Kings 7:14","segments":["They took therefore two chariot horses; and the king sent after the host of the Syrians, saying, Go and see."],"ref":"II Kings 7:14","verse":14,"words":[{"text":"They took","strong":"H3947"},{"text":" therefore two","strong":"H8147"},{"text":" chariot","strong":"H7393"},{"text":" horses","strong":"H5483"},{"text":"; and the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" sent","strong":"H7971"},{"text":" after","strong":"H310"},{"text":" the host","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Go","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" and see","strong":"H7200"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9722,"title":"II Kings 7:15","segments":["And they went after them unto Jordan: and, lo, all the way [was] full of garments and vessels, which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. And the messengers returned, and told the king."],"ref":"II Kings 7:15","verse":15,"words":[{"text":"And they went","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" after","strong":"H310"},{"text":" them unto Jordan","strong":"H3383"},{"text":": and, lo, all the way","strong":"H1870"},{"text":" [was] full","strong":"H4392"},{"text":" of garments","strong":"H899"},{"text":" and vessels","strong":"H3627"},{"text":", which the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":" had cast away","strong":"H7993"},{"text":" in their haste","strong":"H2648"},{"text":". And the messengers","strong":"H4397"},{"text":" returned","strong":"H7725"},{"text":", and told","strong":"H5046"},{"text":" the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9723,"title":"II Kings 7:16","segments":["And the people went out, and spoiled the tents of the Syrians. So a measure of fine flour was [sold] for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD."],"ref":"II Kings 7:16","verse":16,"words":[{"text":"And the people","strong":"H5971"},{"text":" went out","strong":"H3318"},{"text":", and spoiled","strong":"H962"},{"text":" the tents","strong":"H4264"},{"text":" of the Syrians","strong":"H758"},{"text":". So a measure","strong":"H5429"},{"text":" of fine flour","strong":"H5560"},{"text":" was [sold] for a shekel","strong":"H8255"},{"text":", and two measures","strong":"H5429"},{"text":" of barley","strong":"H8184"},{"text":" for a shekel","strong":"H8255"},{"text":", according to the word","strong":"H1697"},{"text":" of the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9724,"title":"II Kings 7:17","segments":["And the king appointed the lord on whose hand he leaned to have the charge of the gate: and the people trode upon him in the gate, and he died, as the man of God had said, who spake when the king came down to him."],"ref":"II Kings 7:17","verse":17,"words":[{"text":"And the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" appointed","strong":"H6485"},{"text":" the lord","strong":"H7991"},{"text":" on whose hand","strong":"H3027"},{"text":" he leaned","strong":"H8172"},{"text":" to have the charge of the gate","strong":"H8179"},{"text":": and the people","strong":"H5971"},{"text":" trode","strong":"H7429"},{"text":" upon him in the gate","strong":"H8179"},{"text":", and he died","strong":"H4191"},{"text":", as the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":" had said","strong":"H1696"},{"text":", who spake","strong":"H1696"},{"text":" when the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" came down","strong":"H3381"},{"text":" to him."}]},{"id":9725,"title":"II Kings 7:18","segments":["And it came to pass as the man of God had spoken to the king, saying, Two measures of barley for a shekel, and a measure of fine flour for a shekel, shall be to morrow about this time in the gate of Samaria:"],"ref":"II Kings 7:18","verse":18,"words":[{"text":"And it came to pass as the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":" had spoken","strong":"H1696"},{"text":" to the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Two measures","strong":"H5429"},{"text":" of barley","strong":"H8184"},{"text":" for a shekel","strong":"H8255"},{"text":", and a measure","strong":"H5429"},{"text":" of fine flour","strong":"H5560"},{"text":" for a shekel","strong":"H8255"},{"text":", shall be to morrow","strong":"H4279"},{"text":" about this time","strong":"H6256"},{"text":" in the gate","strong":"H8179"},{"text":" of Samaria","strong":"H8111"},{"text":":"}]},{"id":9726,"title":"II Kings 7:19","segments":["And that lord answered the man of God, and said, Now, behold, [if] the LORD should make windows in heaven, might such a thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof."],"ref":"II Kings 7:19","verse":19,"words":[{"text":"And that lord","strong":"H7991"},{"text":" answered","strong":"H6030"},{"text":" the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":", and said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Now, behold, [if] the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" should make","strong":"H6213"},{"text":" windows","strong":"H699"},{"text":" in heaven","strong":"H8064"},{"text":", might such a thing","strong":"H1697"},{"text":" be? And he said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Behold, thou shalt see","strong":"H7200"},{"text":" it with thine eyes","strong":"H5869"},{"text":", but shalt not eat","strong":"H398"},{"text":" thereof."}]},{"id":9727,"title":"II Kings 7:20","segments":["And so it fell out unto him: for the people trode upon him in the gate, and he died."],"ref":"II Kings 7:20","verse":20,"words":[{"text":"And so it fell out unto him: for the people","strong":"H5971"},{"text":" trode","strong":"H7429"},{"text":" upon him in the gate","strong":"H8179"},{"text":", and he died","strong":"H4191"},{"text":"."}]}]}
